# Task flow

## Task Execution Flow UI Interaction

### Phase 1: Task Initiation & API Request
  - User input (etc. show me all instances with dfa-crc)
  - Start API request with the user's message content, formatted as:
```
<task>show me all instances with dfa-crc</task>
</environment_detail>User info...; System info...</environment_detail>
```
 - Display a loading icon indicator with "API Request..." title
 - Show the API request content in a formatted code block

### Phase 2: Tool Approval Request
- When AI responds with a tool call:
  - Display a tool icon before the title
  - Show the tool name and parameters in a formatted code block
  - Display other additional context from the AI response
  - Add a "Waiting for user approval..." status text
  - Show "Approve" and "Reject" buttons at the bottom of the entire ChatBox component

### Phase 3: Tool Execution & Result
- After user approval:
  - Show a loading indicator during tool execution
  - Display the tool execution result in a formatted manner
  - Indicate that results are being sent back to the AI

### Phase 4: Task Completion
- When AI responds without tool calls:
  - Display a check icon with "Task Completed" title
  - Show the AI response content in a properly formatted message